 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are in the data
+file as `apiKeys` (`docs/DATA.md`); each has a role:
+
+- `viewer` may only read (every `GET` route except `GET /audit`).
+- `cook` may also cook recipes (`POST /recipes/:id/cook`), record waste
+  (`POST /batches/:id/waste`), log temperatures (`POST /temperatures`) and
+  enter stock-take counts (`POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`).
+- `manager` may do everything.
+
+A request without a key or with an unknown key gets 401 `unauthorized`
+(whatever the route); a known key that may not use the route gets 403
+`forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request that is not a read (`POST`, `PUT`, ...) and carries a known
+key writes an audit entry, whatever its outcome:
+
+    { "id": 7, "at": "2026-10-28T10:00:00.000Z", "keyName": "Dev cook",
+      "method": "POST", "path": "/recipes/1/cook", "status": 200 }
+
+`GET /audit` lists the entries newest first and is for managers only.
+Requests answered with 401 are not audited (there is no key to name).
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
